'''Group E of the 1994 FIFA World Cup''' was one of six groups of four teams competing at the [[1994 FIFA World Cup|1994 World Cup]] in the [[United States]]. The first match was played June 18, 1994, and the final games took place simultaneously on June 28, 1994.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/tournaments/archive/worldcup/usa1994/index.html|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20131220184449/http://www.fifa.com/tournaments/archive/worldcup/usa1994/index.html|url-status=dead|archive-date=December 20, 2013|title=1994 FIFA World Cup USA|publisher=fifa.com|accessdate=July 31, 2014}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/94full.html|title=World Cup 1994|website=[[RSSSF]]|accessdate=July 31, 2014}}</ref>

The group consisted of [[Italy national football team|Italy]], [[Republic of Ireland national football team|Republic of Ireland]],  [[Mexico national football team|Mexico]], and [[Norway national football team|Norway]]. Mexico won the group on goals scored. Ireland and Italy also progressed to the knockout rounds, having finished with identical records and the Irish team qualifying in second place as a result of their victory against the Italians. The Italians qualified as one of the best-scoring third place teams. Norway's shortcomings in attack ultimately let them down, and they exited the tournament with only one goal. It is the only group in World Cup history in which all four teams finished with the same number of points, and all the teams even had the same goal difference.

It is also the most difficult group in World Cup since FIFA ranking debuted in 1992, measured in terms of average FIFA ranking. The average FIFA ranking of the four teams was 10 (Italy 4, Norway 6, Ireland 14 and Mexico 16).<ref>[https://www.instagram.com/p/DR0GguQkr1b/?igsh=bGNweTJ2NTRnZHZt Fox Sports: Hardest group in each FIFA  World Cup by FIFA rank]</ref>

