===Italy vs Republic of Ireland===
[[Ray Houghton]]'s early goal proved the only one of the match where Ireland's defense prevailed over Italy's attack.<ref>[https://www.theguardian.com/observer/irelandfootball/story/0,,587032,00.html The Observer: One giant step for the Irish]</ref><ref>[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4gtZnyCDljE Rep of Ireland v Italy 1994 Full Game]</ref> During the game, members of the [[Ulster Volunteer Force]] (UVF), a [[Ulster loyalism|loyalist]] paramilitary group, burst into a [[public house|pub]] in [[Northern Ireland]] with [[assault rifle]]s and fired on the customers,<ref name="UVF atrocities">[https://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/uk_news/northern_ireland/6617329.stm "The UVF's catalogue of atrocities"] . [[BBC News]]. June 18, 2009.</ref> killing six civilians and wounding five. The pub was targeted because it was frequented mainly by Catholics,<ref name="The Economist">''[[The Economist]]'' newspaper. June 25, 1994. pp. 25–26. "For the 24 fans gathered in Heights Bar in the quiet village of Loughinisland in County Down, the cheering was followed by carnage. Two men walked into the pub and sprayed the room with bullets, killing six and wounding five, and then fled laughing. The Ulster Volunteer Force, a Protestant terrorist group, later claimed it had carried out the attack. It chose the pub only because it knew that those gathered to support Ireland's team would be Catholic".</ref> and was crowded with supporters watching the [[Republic of Ireland national football team|Republic of Ireland]].<ref name="The Economist"/> It is thus sometimes called the "World Cup massacre" or the [[Loughinisland massacre]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.irishtimes.com/news/ireland/irish-news/six-men-dead-the-world-cup-massacre-1.1831478 |title=Six men dead: the World Cup massacre |date=June 14, 2014 |first1=Keith |last1=Duggan |website=irishtimes.com |accessdate=June 28, 2024}}</ref><ref>[https://www.independent.co.uk/news/six-shot-dead-in-ulster-world-cup-massacre-1423674.html "Six shot dead in Ulster World Cup massacre"] {{Webarchive |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180422062222/https://www.independent.co.uk/news/six-shot-dead-in-ulster-world-cup-massacre-1423674.html |date=April 22, 2018 }}. [[The Independent]]. June 19, 1994.</ref><ref>[http://www.irishcentral.com/news/1994-world-cup-massacre-of-irish-fans-by-loyalists-will-be-major-espn-movie-239814941-240124801.html "1994 World Cup massacre of Irish fans by Loyalists will be major ESPN movie"] {{Webarchive |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140714114318/http://www.irishcentral.com/news/1994-world-cup-massacre-of-irish-fans-by-loyalists-will-be-major-espn-movie-239814941-240124801.html |date=July 14, 2014 }}. IrishCentral. January 12, 2014.</ref>

